# --- DISCOVERIES 10-24 (optional, no quest needs them): camp + note; TP_SnowVehicle02 + chest; hatch with a chest; buried treasure; viewpoint ---
place campfire_1 - at 26.4 32.6 ground sit
place Balboa_DecorationPrefabBase_SimpleTent - at 29.4 34.6 ground sit yaw=137
place "Box Small" - at 24.4 35.1 ground sit
place Note_Paper dnote at 24.4 35.1 ground y=1.6 drop yaw=20
note dnote Good Morning, Ice! - callers | GOOD MORNING, ICE! - CALLER LOG, T. HALLEN (SPARKS)\n\nOn air at seven, every day, from this tent - the council took my mast but not my battery.\nCaller 38: the Iron Whale. A woman reading the ice like a weather forecast. Lovely voice. Gone in four seconds.\nCaller 39: nobody. Static. I played it a record anyway.\nCaller 40: a seal. Barked twice. I counted it.\nCaller 41: a penguin. Said nothing. Best caller this week.\nCaller 42: the courier's dogs, howling down the line while he was by with the post. He asked me very nicely to switch off. I asked him very nicely who was asking.\nNote for the council: it is not broadcasting if nobody answers. It is talking to the ice, and the ice has never once complained.
place Note_Paper sparksbye at 25.2 34.4 ground y=0.75 drop yaw=300
note sparksbye Sparks' farewell | SPARKS' FAREWELL - pinned inside the tent flap\n\nTo whoever comes looking, and to the council, who will not:\nYou banished me for talking. Fair enough. It is the only thing I was ever any good at.\nI am taking the small raft and Bramble, who is a llama and therefore the most sensible member of this city. She has packed nothing and is calm about it. I have packed the set, two batteries and the best of the QSL cards the stations sent me over the years. The rest are in the box by the fire. Keep them; they prove we were all here once, and talking.\nI will go on air at seven wherever the ice drops me. If you hear Good Morning, Ice on a band you were not expecting, that is me - still not dead, still not quiet.\n- Tor Hallen
place Loot_ChestSmall sparkscards at 27.6 31.4 ground sit yaw=210
note sparkscards Sparks' card box | Sparks' card box: QSL cards from every station, and one penguin.
loot sparkscards CopperIngot*2;Plastic*2;TradeToken*1
prop sparkscards loot.refill=0
place Zone_Trigger sparkszone at 26.4 34 ground y=1
prop sparkszone zone.id=sparks_tent
prop sparkszone zone.radius=4
prop sparkszone zone.repeat=never
prop sparkszone zone.message=A tent on the ice, a car battery, a wire up a pole. Somebody went on broadcasting out here.
place TP_SnowVehicle02 dvan at -26.4 -32.6 ground yaw=257
prop dvan tint.color=#7a8a96
prop dvan tint.amount=0.5
place Loot_ChestSmall dwreckchest at -30.4 -29.6 ground sit yaw=197
note dwreckchest Driver's box | Under the driver's seat: bolts, glass, a scrap of leather.
loot dwreckchest Bolt*2;Glass*2;Leather*2
prop dwreckchest loot.refill=0
call hatchcache x=-15 z=-12 r=8 seed=12791 alias=dhatch chest=dhatchchest items=MetalIngot*2;Wool*3;Bolt*2
call vinecache x=-12 z=15 r=15 seed=12793 chest=dvinechest vines=dvines items=Rope*3;Wool*2;Bolt*3
call treasure x=-39.7 z=13.7 r=15 n=1 seed=12792
prop treasure12792 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*2;MetalOre*2
place Zone_Trigger dview at -15.1 39.2 ground
prop dview zone.id=saga_drift_view
prop dview zone.radius=7
prop dview zone.repeat=never
prop dview zone.message=Nine old ships frozen into one sheet of ice, their masts like a winter forest.

# --- Settings, story item, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Saga Drift
info author=Custom Islands
info description=Nine old whaling ships lashed hull to hull and frozen into the ice: a city with plank streets, a smelter yard, a council cabin, a chapel - and no one in it but rats and screechers. The seventh island of The Frozen Horizon.
island on.arrive=message||Nine masts in the fog, and not a light among them. The best radio on the white sea - silent.

story chapelcode|The chapel's code|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|You typed the charter's year into the chapel strongbox's keypad.

note charter City charter | SAGA DRIFT - CITY CHARTER\n\nNine keels, one city. Signed on the ice in the year 1909, when the last ship was lashed.\nNo ship leaves alone. No light goes out alone. The radio belongs to all.\n\n(the chapel keeps the city's strongbox; its lock is set to the year of this charter)
note minutes Council cabin minutes | COUNCIL OF SAGA DRIFT - MINUTES, KEPT BY THE CLERK, R. AAS\n\nItem 1: the order from the Coldhold, come by the courier's dog sledge, sealed. The Warden writes: all comms off, every band, so the signal from the south will not find us. Carried, five to four. The radio was shut down the same night.\nItem 2: the Whale to be told nothing. Not carried. The Whale was sent north on our band anyway - on the Coldhold's order, in our voice. The clerk notes his shame.\nItem 3: Tor Hallen, called Sparks, found broadcasting from a tent on the ice outside the ships, against Item 1, for the fourth time. Banished. He asked to take the llama. Carried, nine to nothing; nobody else will feed her.\nItem 4: the rendering house is full of rats again.
note sermon Last sermon | (the chaplain's last sermon, on the lectern - Father Ansgar)\n\nWe were nine ships because no ship can live alone up here. We lashed our keels and promised each other: no light goes out alone.\nNow the vault asks us to be silent for its sake. A seed bank under the glacier, they say, for when the world is green again. The Warden is afraid of something in the south. So am I. I am afraid of it the way I am afraid of the dark - which is to say, I light a candle and keep talking.\nWe sent Tor away for singing to penguins. God forgive us, the penguins miss him.\nI say a city that stops talking is already dead.\nThe glacier is on 1000. Go and see what they are keeping.
note flensechest Smelter yard chest | Smelter yard chest: the electric smelter's plans, for when the generator runs.
note councilchest Council chest | The council's chest: beets from the planter boxes, the city's seal.
note renderchest Rendering house chest | Rendering house chest: the advanced biofuel extractor's plans, oil-stained.
note chapelbox Chapel strongbox | The city's treasury in tokens, the chaplain's prayer book.
note anchorchest Winch locker | Winch locker: the advanced anchor's plans - it held nine ships.
loot flensechest Blueprint_SmelterElectric*1;MetalIngot*2;Scrap*3
prop flensechest loot.refill=0
loot councilchest Raw_Beet*4;Plank*6;Rope*2
prop councilchest loot.refill=0
loot renderchest Blueprint_BiofuelExtractorAdvanced*1;Leather*2;Bolt*2
prop renderchest loot.refill=0
loot chapelbox TradeToken*6;MetalIngot*2;Raw_Beet*2
prop chapelbox loot.refill=0
loot anchorchest Blueprint_AnchorStationaryAdvanced*1;MetalIngot*2;Rope*4
prop anchorchest obj.name=anchorchest
prop anchorchest beh.hidden=1
prop bell1 obj.name=bell1
prop bell1 beh.use=Ring the gangway ship's bell
prop bell1 if.use=!signal|bell1
prop bell1 on.use=signal||bell1\ngive||story:bellrung*1\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/keypad/keypad_correct\nmessage||The bell clangs over the ice. Far off, something creaks on the flagship's bow.
prop bell2 obj.name=bell2
prop bell2 beh.use=Ring the middle ship's bell
prop bell2 if.use=!signal|bell2
prop bell2 on.use=signal||bell2\ngive||story:bellrung*1\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/keypad/keypad_correct\nmessage||A second bell. The ice round the anchor cracks.
prop bell3 obj.name=bell3
prop bell3 beh.use=Ring the far ship's bell
prop bell3 if.use=!signal|bell3
prop bell3 on.use=signal||bell3\ngive||story:bellrung*1\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/keypad/keypad_correct\nmessage||The third bell - the city's old 'all hands'. The winch is ready to turn.
story bellrung|A ship's bell rung|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|One of the three bells of the city's "all hands".
story winchfree|The anchor winch freed|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The flagship's winch turns again.
prop anchorwinch obj.name=anchorwinch
prop anchorwinch beh.use=Turn the anchor winch
prop anchorwinch if.use=take|story:pawl|1\ntake|story:bellrung|3
prop anchorwinch on.use=give||story:winchfree*1\nshow|anchorchest\nmessage||The chain groans and comes up a link at a time. The winch locker under it is free.
prop anchorwinch else.use=message||Frozen by order: "THE WINCH TURNS ON ALL HANDS ONLY." Three bells call all hands - one on each of three hulls. And the winch's pawl is gone: the harbour master's ledger will say where.
prop dhatchchest if.open=wears|HeadLight*
prop dhatchchest else.open=message||A ship's hold under the hatch, pitch black - wear a headlight.
prop anchorchest loot.refill=0
prop treasure12051 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*3

# --- DEEP 10-24: the pawl, the ledger, the extras ---
story pawl|The winch's pawl|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The anchor winch's iron pawl - without it the chain runs free.
note ledger Harbour master's ledger | HARBOUR MASTER'S LEDGER - K. VIK\n\nThe Coldhold's order came with the post: the anchor winch is not to turn, so no ship leaves to carry word south. I took its pawl out myself.\nThe old harbour crane on the berg went over in the January gale, jib first, down the far side. Its cab lies split on the top, where no one goes now. I carried the pawl up there on my own two feet, wrapped it in the city flag and put it in the cab's chest. Then I sat in the wreck and cried a bit, which the ledger need not record, and does.\nThe city's all hands is three bells. With the bells rung and the pawl back, the winch turns.\nLast line: the tenth ship went down in the lead the winter we signed. We do not count her. We should.
note cranecab Crane cab chest | The fallen crane's cab: the winch's pawl, wrapped in a flag.
loot cranecab story:pawl*1;MetalIngot*2;Rope*2
prop cranecab loot.refill=0
note bergcavechest Harbour office chest | Harbour master's chest: harbour dues in tokens, and his dry socks.
loot bergcavechest TradeToken*3;Wool*2;Bolt*2
prop bergcavechest loot.refill=0
note netnote Net mender's note | (pinned to the net loft's table - INGRID, NET MENDER)\n\nNets for nine ships, and one for the tenth that no one mends. I mend it anyway, every spring, a few knots at a time, in case she comes up.\nMy husband says I am mad. My husband also says the Warden is a great man, so I take his opinions the way I take the tide.\nThe radio is off, and the city is so quiet you can hear the ice talking under the hulls. It does not say anything kind.\nThe good twine is in the crate by the door. Take what you need. Mend something.
note netcrate Net loft crate | The net loft's crate: twine, floats, a mender's needle.
loot netcrate Rope*4;Plastic*3;Nail*6
prop netcrate loot.refill=0
note tenthchest Tenth ship's strongbox | Fourteen metres down: the tenth ship's charter, signed 1908, her captain's purse.
loot tenthchest TitaniumIngot*1;MetalIngot*3;TradeToken*4
prop treasure12741 treasure.loot=MetalOre*3;CopperOre*2

